  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#6756\", \"PowerToys#5374\", \"PowerToys#45021\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been made before. The main tracking ticket is PowerToys#6756, \\\"App-specific remapping for keys\\\". Other tickets, including #5374 and #45021, were closed as duplicates of it. Keyboard Manager's \\\"Remap keys\\\" currently works globally only. Only \\\"Remap shortcuts\\\" lets you pick a target app. No app-specific key remap has been delivered in these tickets. Add a 👍 reaction and your use case to #6756. For your Enter-key scenario, a workaround is to use \\\"Remap shortcuts\\\" with a target app, but it needs a modifier-based shortcut. A plain Enter key can't be remapped for one app that way. Until the feature is built, you would need a third-party tool, such as AutoHotkey or Keyboard Butler, for app-specific single-key remaps.\"}",
